bpftune (0.4.28) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Add loss rate as a metric axis.  metric is now
    rtt_term + rate_term + loss_term, where loss_term =
    min(retrans/segs_out, LOSS_CAP_BP) / LOSS_CAP_BP * LOSS_SCALE
    with LOSS_CAP_BP=200 (2.00%).  The met log line gains a loss=
    field so the distribution can be observed live.
  * Remove the hardcoded forced-BBR rescue in RETRANS_CB.  It
    predated the per-destination metric and bypassed it: any
    socket above ~1.56% loss was switched to BBR and its RTT_CB
    flag cleared, so lossy sockets could never vote for any other
    algorithm.  With loss now in the metric, the tuner can learn
    per-path which algorithm handles loss best; the forced BBR
    shortcut is no longer needed.  The TCP_THIN_LINEAR_TIMEOUTS
    opt-in for lossy sockets is kept.
  * STATE_VERSION 6 -> 7 (metric formula changed; old bucket
    values are not comparable).  State file MUST be deleted on
    deploy.

 -- Christophe Deppe <cddeppe@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 14 Sep 2026 14:00:00 +0200

bpftune (0.4.27) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Re-anchor best_i/best_v on every ESTABLISHED.  The incremental
    tracker in the vote path only compares best against second, so a
    third algorithm can drift into a lower position without ever being
    promoted through the pair.  Observed on the fleet as best_i
    disagreeing with the top-3 output.  Fix persists minindex and
    metric_min (already computed by the existing selection loop) into
    remote_host->best_i/best_v.  No new variables — an earlier attempt
    with an explicit min2index blew the 1M insn verifier budget.

 -- Christophe Deppe <cddeppe@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 14 Sep 2026 15:00:00 +0200

bpftune (0.4.26) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Merge vote+swap back to a single RTT_CB program.  set_cong is now
    called inline from the vote path, removing the pending_swap field
    and the cross-program queue.  Swaps fire in the same RTT_CB event
    as the decision instead of on a later event.  Program count: 3 -> 2.
  * METRIC_TRIGGER_SEGS 5000 -> 10000.  The 5K experiment biased the
    metric: every socket 5K sample is roughly 10x lower than its 25K
    sample, so 5K samples dominated the leader ranking and cubic
    took over on n=1.
  * MIN_LEADER_TRUST=3.  A leader needs at least 3 votes before it
    can be a swap target.
  * No downgrade branch.  A socket already on best_i has no better
    target and is skipped; previously the code targeted second_i, a
    strict downgrade that could thrash between best and second-best.
  * SWAP_BAD_FIRST=1, SWAP_BAD_LATER=2.  First rescue fires on a
    single bad checkpoint (faster rescue for 30s+ videos); subsequent
    swaps still require two, to prevent thrash.
  * STATE_VERSION 5 -> 6: pending_swap removed.  State file must be
    deleted on deploy.

 -- Christophe Deppe <cddeppe@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 14 Sep 2026 05:00:00 +0200

bpftune (0.4.25) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Mid-socket algorithm swap: when a socket is assigned a bottom-half
    algorithm at ESTABLISHED (rank_at_assign >= 8), and its metric stays
    >= 1.25x the best alternative for 2 consecutive voting checkpoints,
    swap it to that alternative via bpf_setsockopt(TCP_CONGESTION) from
    a dedicated RTT_CB program.  Protects against exploration regret:
    the ~5% of sockets greedy assigns to a random algorithm no longer
    stay on a bad pick for their entire life.  Bounded by MAX_SWAPS=2
    and a 5s settle window after each swap.
  * Split the single sockops program into three (conn_tuner /
    conn_tuner_vote / conn_tuner_swap).  The merged program with the
    swap decision in RTT_CB exceeded the 1M instruction verifier
    budget via state explosion: a 16-iter loop adjacent to two live
    map_value pointers plus helper calls.  Snapshotting best_alt_i at
    ESTABLISHED removes all loops from the vote path; the swap exec
    path is straight-line.
  * sk_storage_map value type: __u64 -> struct conn_state { state,
    swaps, bad_count, settle_until, pending_swap, best_alt_i,
    rank_at_assign }.

  Userspace attaches and detaches all three programs at the same
  cgroup sockops hook.

 -- Christophe Deppe <cddeppe@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 13 Sep 2026 23:00:00 +0200

