bpftune (0.4.18) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Switch bucket key from next-hop gateway to destination IP, matching
    the metric's stated intent (per remote host).  Previously all IPv4
    traffic through the default route shared one bucket, mixing fast
    local CDN paths with slow tunnel paths.
  * Switch remote_host_map to LRU hash, 4096 entries.  Self-manages
    eviction on a destination-keyed workload.
  * Persist only buckets with >= PERSIST_MIN_INSTANCES (8) connections.
    Recurring paths survive restarts; one-off destinations do not.
  * Bump STATE_VERSION to 2: prior state files held gateway-addressed
    keys, which are meaningless under destination keying.

